    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d920">

                <pb facs="1252" n="1240" sameAs="frus:frus1945v06/pg1240"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">892.01/12–3044: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Hurley</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extracts]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-12-30T08:00:00+07:00">December 30,
                            1944—8 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 12:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2086. Foreign Office informs us in strict confidence that two groups of Thai
                    nationals, one civil and one military, have arrived in Kunming secretly from
                    Thailand for talks with Chinese Government officials and that head of civil
                    group bears an autographed letter from Thai Premier.<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d920-f1"/> Foreign Office desires to ascertain views of American
                    Government as to how to deal with the delegation and what general lines of
                    policy should be pursued. Foreign Office states arrangements will be made in due
                    course after delegation’s arrival in Chungking for us to meet them informally
                    and is making similar approach to British Embassy.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . .</p>
                <p>Foreign Office states no objection to informing Thai Minister.<anchor n="4"
                        xml:id="d920-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>Please instruct.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hurley</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
